{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339046-mobile-caerns-in-werewolf-are-they-possible","id":1339046,"title":"\"Mobile Caerns\" in Werewolf: Are they possible?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-02T12:54:43-07:00","id":1339046,"title":"\"Mobile Caerns\" in Werewolf: Are they possible?","content":"This one is another doozy.<br /> <br /> Is it theoretically possible to build a Caern that has the ability to move or change locations? The only real example of note is from First Edition, where the Black Spiral Dancers turned MIR into a Hive, while it was still in orbit. This in essence granted a Moon Bridge to Spess.<br /> <br /> The question then is, could the Gaian Garou mimic such an eccentricity on their own terms? Examples might include turning a decomissioned train, private superyacht, etc. into a Caern, with the bawn being a mobile perimeter of sorts. (One hypothetical case would be a Dark Ages game where a Sept of Mongolian Shadow Lords have a Great Tent, and a perimeter of wagons).<br /> <br /> And yes, I know General Lee allows *vehicles* to be Pack Totems. This is more a matter of spiritual scaling-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-04T21:16:00-07:00","id":1339520,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would be possible to use a vehicle as a basis for a Caern. That being said a Caern who moves to certain locations across a vast area would not be unreasonable. I'd also point out there are Living Caerns in the ocean in whales.. though I'm not sure how applicable that would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T17:18:19-07:00","id":1339729,"title":"","content":"Some random thoughts:<br /> <br /> There is a VW Bus that is a Node in a MtA supplement, iirc.<br /> <br /> I would think that such a caern would be a unique thing.<br /> <br /> Given, that a Caern/Sept guideline in &quot;Guardians of the Caerns&quot; would include the design of a bawn, gathering area, login area, shrines and such, the &quot;mobile&quot; caern would be a mobile heart of a caern, and not a complete thing.<br /> <br /> A airplane carrier is its own city basically, and moving, so there could be a whole sept on it and a mobile caern was possible, essentially....<br /> <br /> Tectonic plates aren't stationary, either...<br /> <br /> A &quot;pyramid corner stone fetish&quot; would create a caern-like area if activated.<br /> <br /> We have a caern in our LAPR game, that has it's heart moving around it a limited area. The garou always have their moots in the gathering area / loging area next to its current position. That's how we rationalise different locations for our game.<br /> <br /> I could imagine a mobile sept with a caern, like a circus or similar mobile group.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T09:16:56-07:00","id":1341456,"title":"","content":"Since you already mentioned the Spirals: There's the Trinity Hive, located in the bowels of Grammaw, the largest known Thunderwyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-17T08:45:44-07:00","id":1341869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339046-mobile-caerns-in-werewolf-are-they-possible?p=1339729#post1339729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some random thoughts:<br /> <br /> There is a VW Bus that is a Node in a MtA supplement, iirc.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not all Nodes are acceptable as Caerns. I'd argue a Gaian Caern needs some physical connection to Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T00:37:12-07:00","id":1342034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339046-mobile-caerns-in-werewolf-are-they-possible?p=1341869#post1341869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all Nodes are acceptable as Caerns. I'd argue a Gaian Caern needs some physical connection to Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I just wrote my random thoughts on the matter....<br /> <br /> Outsite of the Rokea-Subsetting, which has mobile caerns like you pointed out, I would think that caerns are stationary. Can't really imagine it otherwise. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure if the stargazers with their sept inside the Atherial Realm have a Caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T10:45:03-07:00","id":1342119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339046-mobile-caerns-in-werewolf-are-they-possible?p=1341456#post1341456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you already mentioned the Spirals: There's the Trinity Hive, located in the bowels of Grammaw, the largest known Thunderwyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, I think that the Spirals have an Hive in a Satellite in Rage Across Russia. Technically, that's a mobile caern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T11:07:07-07:00","id":1342130,"title":"","content":"Yup. Mentioned it in the original post: MIR the Russian space station was actually a Spiral Hive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T19:09:48-07:00","id":1342251,"title":"","content":"I had a thought rethinking the Rokea Whale Caerns. That what basically keeps Modern fera from having the equivalent is lack of Dinosaurs, BUT what about masses of smaller organisms? Like the Great Herds of Buffallo the Millions of Passenger Pidgeons etc.. that perhaps there once were land based ones that have been lost as numbers are depleted and species go extinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T16:44:41-07:00","id":1342604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1339046-mobile-caerns-in-werewolf-are-they-possible?p=1339729#post1339729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A airplane carrier is its own city basically, and moving, so there could be a whole sept on it and a mobile caern was possible...</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. Even the Glass Walkers scraping together enough money to buy an aircraft carrier (never mind <i>maintain</i> it), would be rather ambitious. Getting a hold of an aircraft carrier would also pose some problems. Even if they were to pick up a small-<i>ish</i> one that was set to be scrapped (like INS <i>Vikrant</i> a few years back), people would notice. When the PRC picked up H.M.A.S. <i>Melbourne</i> supposedly for scrap, every naval intelligence agency on earth was wondering within a year just <i>why</i> it was taking the Chinese so long to dispose of her (Although &quot;buying used&quot; would mean that the ship had developed some degree of spiritual presence -- and being named would also give it a degree of personality that together would make the spiritual side of caern opening more feasible). Aircraft carriers are just about the ultimate in screaming &quot;PAY ATTENTION TO ME!!!&quot;. Not good if you're werewolves trying to maintain a low profile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">There's the Trinity Hive, located in the bowels of Grammaw, the largest known Thunderwyrm.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Ah. Beat me to it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: So, anyway, the point I'd like to make is mobile caerns should be <i>possible</i> -- but rare. And normal caerns are already pretty darned rare to begin with.</span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 10-20-2019, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}